  "id": "intracarotid-amobarbital-procedure",
  "term": "intracarotid amobarbital procedure",
  "definition": "The intracarotid amobarbital procedure is an invasive test used before epilepsy surgery to determine which side of the brain is dominant for language. In this context, it is treated as the standard method against which noninvasive language-lateralization tests are compared.",
